  "runId": "32125726287",
  "runUrl": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/actions/runs/32125726287",
  "collectedAtUtc": "2026-08-18T10:15:21.973Z",
  "approved": false,
  "reviewDecision": null,
  "approvals": [],
  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aEHcn",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3803040124,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 241,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3803040124",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This treats all non-2xx responses (including a legitimate 404 when the document is missing) as an InvalidOperationException, which prevents the controller’s `response is null ? Status.NotFound : Status.OK` path from ever being used. Consider handling `HttpStatusCode.NotFound` explicitly (e.g., return null / a not-found result) and reserving the exception for policy/redirect/technical failures so missing documents map to a controlled 404 as intended.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Valid. RetrieveDocument treated a downstream 404 as an InvalidOperationException, so BookingController returned a technical error and its existing null-to-NotFound mapping was unreachable. The service now returns null for HttpStatusCode.NotFound, the endpoint documents the 404 response, and contract coverage distinguishes missing-document responses from technical failures."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aEHdA",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3803040160,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 227,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3803040160",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "The service validates the URL target, but it never verifies that `request.DocumentId` is consistent with `request.DocumentUrl` (despite the flow/docs indicating 'Verify ID/URL consistency'). This means a mismatched `DocumentId` could be returned while downloading arbitrary allowlisted content. Add a deterministic consistency check (based on the known DMAZE URL shape, e.g., verifying the last path segment contains/ends with the expected `{DocumentId}.pdf` or extracting the document id from the URL path and comparing) and reject mismatches as a controlled bad request.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Valid. The documented download contract requires document-id/document-url consistency, but the service previously trusted the caller-provided ID independently of the allowlisted URL. RetrieveDocument now requires the decoded final path segment to equal {DocumentId}.pdf before DNS resolution or download and maps mismatches to the existing controlled bad-request path; a controller regression test covers the mismatch."
    }
  ],
